// (S-947 (b), S-459.) The line after a line that goes on starts with a run of words before a head (`export fn`,
// §18.1): the head of the run is the start of an item, so it ends the unit that was cut. The run is one
// E0002 (`export` is no part of the head of a declaration), and the item after it is read, so the
// user finds `z_export`. One error in each unit: the `{` that is never closed, and the run of words.

